title: "Figure 7.2.19 - Stream LLM Response with SSE"
---

sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant SessionGW as Session Gateway
    participant TurnCtrl as Turn Controller
    participant OrchSvc as Orchestrator Service
    participant LLMSvc as LLM Service
    participant LLMAPI as Language Model API
    participant TurnRepo as Turn Repository
    participant MessageRepo as Message Repository

    User->>SessionGW: POST /sessions/{id}/turns<br/>Accept: text/event-stream
    SessionGW->>TurnCtrl: Forward request

    Note over TurnCtrl: Establish SSE connection<br/>Keep connection open

    TurnCtrl->>OrchSvc: Process turn
    Note over OrchSvc: Context assembly<br/>Retrieval<br/>Guardrails<br/>(as in Figure 7.2.3)

    OrchSvc->>LLMSvc: Call LLM with streaming
    LLMSvc->>LLMAPI: Request streaming mode
    Note over LLMAPI: Return delta chunks

    loop For each token
        LLMAPI-->>LLMSvc: Token delta
        LLMSvc->>LLMSvc: Buffer token

        LLMSvc->>TurnCtrl: Emit SSE event
        Note over TurnCtrl: event: token<br/>data: {"text": "Hello", "delta": "Hello"}

        TurnCtrl-->>User: Stream token (SSE)
    end

    Note over LLMSvc: Stream completes

    LLMSvc->>OrchSvc: Full response ready
    OrchSvc->>TurnRepo: Create Turn<br/>{role: "assistant", text}
    OrchSvc->>MessageRepo: Create Message

    OrchSvc->>TurnCtrl: Turn complete
    TurnCtrl-->>User: SSE event
    Note over TurnCtrl: event: done<br/>data: {"turnId": "...", "messageId": "..."}

    Note over TurnCtrl: Close SSE connection

    Note over User: Responsive UX:<br/>Text appears gradually<br/>vs waiting for full response
